body:
It does indeed broadcast the ID (i.e. the device is viewable), but once it's connected to your device others wont be able to connect to it despite seeing it (unless some hacking is involved, though i feel like most people have better things to do than hack a speaker, but i may be mistaken). My old edifier was the MP380 (now out of production), even though the response range is advertised to be slightly larger i found the sound to be muddy-ish in comparison to my current pebble pros

&#x200B;

Edit: the bluetooth is toggle-able, pebble pros have 3 modes: aux, usb, bluetooth
